[
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "# Lab 2: the WeatherReading Model and the unit conversion\n\n**Goal:** turn a weather-API answer into a clean reading in °C and °F.\n\n**You will build:**\n1. `WeatherReading`, a Model: the shape of a reading, one field per value.\n2. `ProcessWeather`, an Action: when an answer lands on `campus/weather/raw`, it converts the units and publishes one `WeatherReading` to `campus/weather/reading`.\n\nRun the cells in order: the Action uses the Model."
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 1. The Model\n\n`COLLAPSED` means the Model has no trigger of its own: it publishes only when an Action asks for it with `PUBLISH MODEL`."
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE MODEL WeatherReading COLLAPSED\n    ADD DOUBLE \"temperature_c\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"temperature_f\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"wind_kmh\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"wind_mph\"\n    ADD STRING \"timestamp\""
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## 2. ProcessWeather\n\nIf the answer has no `current.temperature_2m` (for example the API returned an error), the payload goes to `campus/weather/errors` and no reading is published.\n\nWhy test for both `EMPTY` and `\"null\"`? A JSON field that is missing comes back as the text `null`, not as `EMPTY`."
 },
 {
  "kind": 2,
  "language": "lot",
  "value": "DEFINE ACTION ProcessWeather\nON TOPIC \"campus/weather/raw\" DO\n    SET \"temp_raw\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.temperature_2m\" IN PAYLOAD AS STRING)\n    IF {temp_raw} == EMPTY OR {temp_raw} == \"null\" THEN\n        PUBLISH TOPIC \"campus/weather/errors\" WITH PAYLOAD\n    ELSE\n        SET \"temp_c\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.temperature_2m\" IN PAYLOAD AS DOUBLE)\n        SET \"wind_kmh\" WITH (GET JSON \"current.wind_speed_10m\" IN PAYLOAD AS DOUBLE)\n        SET \"temp_f\" WITH (({temp_c} * 9.0 / 5.0) + 32.0)\n        SET \"wind_mph\" WITH ({wind_kmh} * 0.621371)\n        PUBLISH MODEL WeatherReading TO \"campus/weather/reading\" WITH\n            temperature_c = {temp_c}\n            temperature_f = {temp_f}\n            wind_kmh = {wind_kmh}\n            wind_mph = {wind_mph}\n            timestamp = TIMESTAMP \"UTC\""
 },
 {
  "kind": 1,
  "language": "markdown",
  "value": "## Check it worked\n\nThe weather API is not connected yet (that is Lab 3), so pretend to be it. In **Data Viewer → Publish**, publish this to `campus/weather/raw` (Retain off):\n\n```json\n{\"current\": {\"temperature_2m\": 18.4, \"wind_speed_10m\": 12.6}}\n```\n\nA reading appears on `campus/weather/reading` with `temperature_c` 18.4 and `temperature_f` 65.12.\n\nDocs: [MODEL publishing](https://docs.coreflux.org/latest/lot-language/models/publish-model) · [Operations (GET JSON, EMPTY)](https://docs.coreflux.org/latest/lot-language/actions/operations)."
 }
]
